@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ Drafts retain plain text and file, folder, and Session reference chips across Se
 
 A claimed command is one atomic chip at the start of the draft, and the claim lasts exactly as long as that chip. Deleting the arguments and separator keeps the claim. At the chip's edge, the first Backspace or Delete selects the whole chip and the next one removes it and releases the claim, leaving the arguments as plain text; any other key, a click, or a caret move clears the selection. Text or a line break inserted before the chip turns it back into its literal token and releases the claim, and undo restores a deleted chip together with its claim. The persisted draft records the chip's token, so a reload rebuilds the chip once the command catalog resolves the claim; editing the draft first keeps the literal token, which Enter still submits as the command. The same rules apply to every command and locale, including `/goal`, `/目标`, `/plan`, and `/计划`. Command hints and ordinary placeholders remain hidden throughout IME composition and reappear only after the editor commits the final text and the corresponding input is empty.
 
-Workspace selection uses `uiWorkspace.openWorkspace` to prepare the target and commit navigation. Draft content, including structured references, and attachments move in its synchronous preparation callback only while that request is current and no submission is in flight; later navigation, owner disposal, or a submission in flight leaves the original draft in its Session.
+Workspace selection uses `uiWorkspace.openWorkspace` to prepare the target and commit navigation. Draft content, including structured references, and attachments move in its synchronous preparation callback only while that request is current and no submission is in flight; later navigation, owner disposal, or a submission in flight leaves the original draft in its Session. Before the first message, the close button beside the Workspace name calls `openWorkspace(null)` to create an ungrouped Session and carry the draft through the same guarded callback. It does not remove the Workspace or alter existing conversation history.
 
 The package occupies the root-scoped `main` key `conversation`. Its `main.conversation` shell keeps the resident `conversation.header` outside the optional-Session `conversation.content` Component Factory. The header hosts root-scoped navigation without a selected Session; titles, actions, and View tabs remain in its strict Session child. The Factory owns the shared body and Composer, reads the current Session through its standard Hook, and exposes strict-Session `views` plus root-scoped `widthControls` local positions. Its default adapter renders the existing `conversation.session` entry, while the main occurrence selects the width handles; an embedded occurrence can replace `views` and omit those handles without rendering the main Header. The shared body and Composer register the queue and Todo docks. The Todo dock uses the shared panel elevation above the composer; its rows use the shared idle, ongoing, and done markers for pending, in-progress, and completed items. `ctx.uiSession.provide()` materializes the Conversation and input sources from the same Session binding and supplies `inputActions` as a stable standard prop.
 
